--- !u!114 &766445127
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 766445124}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshProUGUI
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Now... wait... something strange just happened. The Principal\u2019s voice
    suddenly choked out, like her power was cut right at the peak of her scream.
    For a second, there was an absolute vacuum in my head\u2014just a void\u2014and
    in that silence, the TV-man leaned forward. He isn\u2019t laughing. He reached
    out his hand toward my face, and his screen suddenly stopped graining.\r\n\r\nA
    video started playing... fuck, I\u2019m looking at it now and my hands are going
    numb. It\u2019s me. It\u2019s actually me, two or three years ago. I\u2019m on
    the playground, dirty, in that torn t-shirt, running with a ball, shouting something
    to the guys, laughing... God, I\u2019m laughing so wildly there, just because
    the sun is shining.\r\n\r\nThen the frame changes\u2014I\u2019m sitting at a
    desk, drawing. Not these ironic diagrams, not these codes... I\u2019m drawing
    dragons, trees, just some random shit that felt important to me back then. I
    loved it. I actually, fucking loved just drawing, before they hammered it into
    my head that everything had to be efficient and structured. I look at that 'me'
    on the screen and I don\u2019t recognize him\u2014he\u2019s alive, he\u2019s
    not a mannequin, there\u2019s no white noise in his eyes.\r\n\r\nI want to touch
    the glass, to pull myself out of there, but the TV-man suddenly gives a slow
    wave, like he\u2019s saying goodbye. The screen instantly collapses into a single
    bright dot, the graininess rushes back, and that ironic whisper returns. Everything
    is gone. I\u2019m sitting here reeling, looking at my trembling fingers, and
    I can\u2019t understand\u2014why do I want to howl right now? What have I done
    to myself?"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 45ae1b20a8af0b947bf46692f07a66b7, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 1302324160900633244, guid: 45ae1b20a8af0b947bf46692f07a66b7, type: 2}
