  _originalText: 
--- !u!114 &970166912
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 970166909}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshProUGUI
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "I went into the school library today. Reeks of old paper and mice. I wanted
    to find something about keeping yourself in check\u2014you know, so I don't snap
    at every dipshit I see. Stumbled upon a book by some Marcus Aurelius guy. An
    emperor or something, I guess. Whatever, that\u2019s not the point.\r\n\r\nAnd
    then, it was like a lightning bolt hit my brain. The Principal\u2019s voice hissed
    right into the back of my skull: <i><size=120%>'Don't touch that garbage. It\u2019s
    weakness. It\u2019s sappy crap for losers who want to justify their own chaos.
    You don\u2019t need reflections\u2014you need STRUCTURE.'</i></size>\r\n\r\nI
    actually dropped the book. The librarian shot me a look like I was plotting a
    terrorist attack. My hands went numb. The voice is right\u2014to hell with these
    old philosophers. It\u2019s just noise for people looking for excuses for their
    mess.\r\nIn the end, I grabbed an 'Encyclopedia for Boys.' You know the type\u2014thick,
    hardcover, teaching you everything from how to tie a tie to how to behave as
    a guest. The Principal\u2019s voice in my head practically purred with satisfaction.
    <i><size=120%>'There. Read. This is how you MUST be. Every action of yours must
    follow the rules.'</i></size>\n\r\nGot home, opened the section on 'proper conduct.'
    I\u2019m looking at the illustrations, and there are these moronic schematic
    stickmen. You know, the ones they draw to show 'good' vs. 'bad.' Stick arms,
    circle heads, stupid smiles on their mugs. It\u2019s peak irony.\r\n<size=80%>I
    stared at one of those 'perfect boys' and suddenly, it hit me. I grabbed a pen
    and started tracing him. Then I drew him another head. And another. They started
    coming out all... crooked, like a kid drew them. Tiny, hideous heads. I defaced
    the whole book. The voice vanished. But I heard this weird laughter.</size>\r\n\r\nI
    found where it was coming from. The TV turned itself on. Bitch. I was home alone.\r\n\r\nFuck
    this."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 45ae1b20a8af0b947bf46692f07a66b7, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 1302324160900633244, guid: 45ae1b20a8af0b947bf46692f07a66b7, type: 2}
  m_fontSharedMaterials: []
  m_fontMaterial: {fileID: 0}
  m_fontMaterials: []
  m_fontColor32:
