  _originalText: 
--- !u!114 &1295805721
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1295805718}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshProUGUI
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "I cupped my fingers like binoculars, looked through the gaps as if through
    a mask, and the letters became sharp. I could read: 'TRUTH,' 'ORDER,' 'LISTEN.'
    The Principal in my head went quiet, as if she were satisfied. Without the mask,
    the world is just noise, blurry shit. But the Mask focuses it. It rips out the
    tongue, yes, but in exchange, you finally see what's real. Only through pain
    can you understand how everything is put together.\n\nWe walked out of the cinema;
    she was yapping about something, laughing... but I looked at her face and saw
    it crumbling into filthy pixels. The Principal whispered: 'She is just noise.'\nI
    got home and I\u2019m writing this now, still reeling. My tongue feels numb,
    but inside, something massive and cold is growing. The TV-head guy is huddled
    in the corner; he\u2019s trembling and fading out."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 45ae1b20a8af0b947bf46692f07a66b7, type: 2}
