--- !u!114 &2013497190
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 2013497187}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshProUGUI
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "History class again. Suffocating. The classroom reeks of a damp rag and
    some kind of old-lady face powder the history teacher wears. She\u2019s been
    droning on for forty minutes about the 'Spring of Nations,' 1848, and all that
    European crap. Seriously, who gives a flying fuck about these bearded guys in
    tricorn hats?\n\n\n\r\nI\u2019m looking at the 8th-grade textbook\u2014on page
    152, there\u2019s this creepy engraving of barricades. People with pitchforks,
    smoke, panic... that\u2019s the only thing that caught my eye. I started tracing
    the smoke with my pen until it looked like real clouds. I wish I were there right
    now, on those barricades, instead of listening to the CHALK screeching against
    the board. That sound is brutal\u2014like they\u2019re scraping my brain.\r\nShe\u2019s
    barking something about revolution, and I\u2019m just staring at her fat ass,
    wishing for this lesson to hurry up and die. She\u2019ll slap me with another
    failing grade because I didn't even open the outline map. God, her breath stinks...\r\n"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 45ae1b20a8af0b947bf46692f07a66b7, type: 2}
